This sentinel file marks the unrenamed template. While it exists, the
template-hygiene check in `buildcore.py` (`_check_template_hygiene`) is
suppressed so the template itself can build its own guide-template.pdf with
placeholders present in README.md and CLAUDE.md.

`bootstrap.py` deletes this file (and itself) after writing the fork's own
title, slug and author into `guide.toml` — which is where every per-guide value
now lives — and re-rendering the `templated` files (pixi.toml, verify.yml,
kit-drift.yml) plus README.md and CLAUDE.md with that identity. No renderer
carries a guide-specific literal, so nothing is substituted into build.py.
